<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
		<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Illum:Param7</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Superfice</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>This program calculates, from a Digital Elevation Model (DEM), the illumination received by a point in the terrain when the Sun occupies a certain position in the celestial sphere. 
</ows:Abstract>
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Calculation of the illumination image from a Digital Elevation Model"/>
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This program calculates, from a Digital Elevation Model (DEM), the illumination received by a point in the terrain when the Sun occupies a certain position in the celestial sphere. This position can be defined."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Option</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Defines the principal options of the pogram:<![CDATA[<ul><li>1: Elevation and azimuth are constant parameters for the file extent.</li><li>2: Elevation and azimuth are raster files.</li><li>
3: Variation of Option 2, where a file of relative solar angles with respect to zenith is specified instead of a file with resepect to the horizon (elevation). The zenith angle and the elevation.</li></ul>]]> 
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1" />
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AllowedValues>
				<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
				</ows:AllowedValues>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MDE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Digital Elevation Model</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Digital Elevation model in the raster format IMG.
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2" />
			<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>		
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Solar Elevation</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>SolarElev</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Value or file which determines the solar elevation (except for Option 3 which uses the zenith angle). If a file is used, it must be a raster file type IMG but not necessarily of the same resolution as the output illumination model.
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4" />
			<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SolarAz</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Solar Azimut </ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Value or file which determines the solar azimuth. If a file is used, it must be a raster file type 
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5" />
			<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>N_neighb_or_degrees</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>N_neighb_or_degrees</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[<ul><li>1: A surface of local tendency of the 1st degree will be defined for each calculation of the normal vector at each point. In this option, the DEM has a greater spatial resolution (smaller pixel size) than the generated illumination model, which inherits the extent and the pixel size of the Reference file.</li><li>2: A surface of local tendency of the 2nd degree will be defined for each calculation of the normal vector at each point. Output conditions are the same as with Option 1.</li><li> 3:A surface of local tendency of the 3rd degree will be defined for each calculation of the normal vector at each point. Output conditions are the same as with Option 1.</li></ul>]]>
</ows:Abstract>
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param6" />
<LiteralData>
			<ows:AllowedValues>
				<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
				</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>		
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Reference</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Reference</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Obligatory parameter for options 1, 2, 3 of the previous N_neighb_or_degrees, which indicates the raster file reference that defines the extent and pixel size of the output illumination model.
</ows:Abstract>
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param7" />
<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MULTIBANDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Multibanda</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If the DEM is multiband (normally of similar extent and different pixel sizes between bands), this parameter indicates that the desired output illumination model will also be multiband.
</ows:Abstract>
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AllowedValues><ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value></ows:AllowedValues>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PREFIX</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Prefix</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Defines a prefix to be affixed to the original file names in order to determine the names of the corrected files in the /MULTIBANDA case. By default this prefix is i_.
</ows:Abstract>
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AnyValue/>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>		
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FACTOR</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>0.01. This parameter is optional (by default the factor is set to 1) and only is applicable to the principal options 2 and 3.
</ows:Abstract>
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AnyValue/>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>		
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>	
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>Result</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>IMG Result</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>IMG result.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3" />
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
		<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Illum:!Param7</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Veïns</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>This option uses neighbors to calculate the normal field.
</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Option</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Defines the principal options of the pogram:<![CDATA[<ul><li>1: Elevation and azimuth are constant parameters for the file extent.</li><li>2: Elevation and azimuth are raster files.</li><li>
3: Variation of Option 2, where a file of relative solar angles with respect to zenith is specified instead of a file with resepect to the horizon (elevation). The zenith angle and the elevation angle are complimentary.</li></ul>]]>
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1" />
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AllowedValues>
				<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
				</ows:AllowedValues>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DEM</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Digital Elevation Model</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Digital Elevation model in the raster format IMG.
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2" />
			<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>		
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SolarElev</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Solar Elevation</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Value or file which determines the solar elevation (except for Option 3 which uses the zenith angle). If a file is used, it must be a raster file type IMG but not necessarily of the same resolution as the output illumination model.
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4" />
			<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SolarAz</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Solar Azimut </ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Value or file which determines the solar azimuth. If a file is used, it must be a raster file type IMG but not necessarily of the same resolution as the output illumination model.
</ows:Abstract>
			<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5" />
			<ComplexData>
				<Default>
					<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Default>
				<Supported>
					<Format>
					<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
				</Supported>
			</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>N_veïns</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Nombre de veïns</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[<ul><li>4: 4 neighbors will be used for the calculation of the normal vector at each point. With this option, the generated illumination model output will be the same resolution and extent as the DEM.</li><li>8: 8 neighbors will be used for the calculation of the normal vector at each point. Output conditions are the same as with the 4 neighbor option.</li></ul>]]>
</ows:Abstract>
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param6" />
<LiteralData>		
			<ows:AllowedValues>
				<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
				<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
				</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>		
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MULTIBANDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Multibanda</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If the DEM is multiband (normally of similar extent and different pixel sizes between bands), this parameter indicates that the desired output illumination model will also be multiband.
</ows:Abstract>
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AllowedValues><ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value></ows:AllowedValues>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PREFIX</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Prefix</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Defines a prefix to be affixed to the original file names in order to determine the names of the corrected files in the /MULTIBANDA case. By default this prefix is i_
</ows:Abstract>
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AnyValue/>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>		
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FACTOR</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract> Indicates the multiplicative factor for the unit values of the elevation, azimuth and degree files. For example, for a raster where the units are decimal degrees, it is necessary to define. 
</ows:Abstract>
			<LiteralData>
				<ows:AnyValue/>
			</LiteralData>
			</Input>		
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>	
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>Result</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>IMG result</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>IMG result.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3" />
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
						<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
						<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
					</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>
